  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "User trust: authentication then authorization",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: protected requests are authenticated by the API Gateway Lambda REQUEST authorizer. Three public Auth routes bypass it; nine routes require it.",
        "CloudFront reads static assets from its private S3 origin via OAC. Only the authorized AWS edition forwarded /api to API Gateway; that forwarding is now removed. S3 never forwards API requests.",
        "API Gateway sends three public Auth routes through its public integration and VPC Link / ALB, without the Lambda authorizer or injected identity. Nine protected routes require the REQUEST authorizer; only their integration overwrites identity headers. The drawing abstracts these internal HTTP transport hops, not their trust gates.",
        "Shipment/Tracking require gateway trust, revalidate the original bearer with Auth and bind the returned user ID. Active-user, role and resource-owner checks remain authoritative.",
        "PROVEN on 29 October: real login/profile, anonymous and invalid-token rejection, cross-user denial and forged-header rejection. Internal HTTP hops are not mTLS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Workload trust: credentials are not interchangeable",
      "items": [
        "Service-account sub and sts.amazonaws.com audience restrict IRSA federation. Tracking publishes events; Shipment consumes SQS; ESO reads approved Secrets Manager values.",
        "ESO writes Kubernetes Secrets. Deployments and migration Jobs consume different secretKeyRef credentials; they do not call ESO as a service.",
        "The credentials-to-database edge represents a consuming pod/Job using TLS and its own schema role. Runtime roles are not migration owners; no browser receives database credentials."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Delivery trust: data, authority and execution",
      "items": [
        "Publisher writes immutable images/build records and release data. Orchestrator dispatches a pinned SSM contract; management separately verifies bytes and expected Helm revision.",
        "GitHub does not directly contact Kubernetes. Management uses its own EKS access/RBAC boundary, not a blanket cluster-admin assignment.",
        "PROVEN: private delivery and automatic recovery. UNVERIFIED: broad production security certification, continuous availability and database migration rollback."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and current state",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: arrows describe source-backed design; the reading guide gives the source for each relationship.",
        "OBSERVED: topology captured on 28–29 October 2026. Runtime retired on 29 October; RDS retained stopped.",
        "PROVEN applies only to named experiments. These diagrams are not live telemetry or a production certification."
      ]
    }
  ],
